{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1452 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "50286bdd8e19eeeb7a24f6d772ba4f8326622c6b09cb3ee2f1309e04110b0e5b" :edb/db-before-t 1451 :edb/db-after-t 1452 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534764 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:15:25.263Z" 13194139534764 true] [17592186229137 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308617 13194139534764 true] [17592186229138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308624 13194139534764 true] [17592186229138 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308631 13194139534764 true] [17592186229139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308638 13194139534764 true] [17592186229139 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308642 13194139534764 true] [17592186308617 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308618 13194139534764 true] [17592186308617 1089 "q-331913" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308617 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534764 true] [17592186308617 1100 "Consider the differential equation \n\n$$\n2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2y=-{x}^{2}-2x+4.\n$$\n\nFind the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." 13194139534764 true] [17592186308617 1113 #uuid "9a519148-1dbb-52b2-8341-8fad4a34af30" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308617 1145 "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $ and $\\gamma ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n2(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+2(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-2x+4\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n2\\alpha {x}^{2}+(4\\alpha +2\\beta )x+(2\\beta +2\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-2x+4.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 4\\alpha +2\\beta =-2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\beta +2\\gamma =4\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2},\\beta =0,\\gamma =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2.\n$$" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308619 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308620 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308621 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308622 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308623 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1041 "selection" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308620 13194139534764 true] [17592186308618 1110 #uuid "c5a2f420-7744-54b9-a957-1e22206a4137" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308619 1034 "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308619 1111 #uuid "63e13ab9-4bd7-5fca-bdbe-a025c1b5a20a" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308620 1034 "-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308620 1111 #uuid "e01b0af9-30cd-50d7-a4ce-8a4cab6010b6" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308621 1034 "-2{x}^{2}" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308621 1111 #uuid "51aa0b61-8028-55c6-8326-35c05b009b18" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308622 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308622 1111 #uuid "353adb76-84b2-5e81-b056-bcf86ce6ad7b" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308623 1034 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308623 1111 #uuid "814c8c66-e968-59ae-9762-36d350fd32ab" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308624 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308625 13194139534764 true] [17592186308624 1089 "q-332550" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308624 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534764 true] [17592186308624 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-{x}^{2}+2x-3.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139534764 true] [17592186308624 1113 #uuid "09b19c17-c03f-56ab-a743-01f7ab8d8701" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308624 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$  we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+2x-3\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha +\\beta )x+(\\beta +\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}+2x-3\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha +\\beta =2\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\beta +\\gamma =-3\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,\\beta =4,\\gamma =-7.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-{x}^{2}+4x-7.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+4x-7.\n$$" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308626 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308627 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308628 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308629 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308630 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1041 "selection" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308629 13194139534764 true] [17592186308625 1110 #uuid "d95ee038-e4e0-565c-9eea-daade6a92927" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308626 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-3{x}^{2}+4x-7" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308626 1111 #uuid "c49dfca2-94c5-548e-9baf-9a2ef97c8f5b" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308627 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+4x+7" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308627 1111 #uuid "29ea374a-ef1b-5dd5-b782-6931263baaee" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308628 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}-4x-7" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308628 1111 #uuid "b5cea147-d03b-5fc5-9000-9eae8db49959" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308629 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+4x-7" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308629 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308629 1111 #uuid "3c3b017d-f699-5661-a43c-7724f21dea07" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308630 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+2x-7" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308630 1111 #uuid "06043398-b0d0-5555-9f49-23528d3e351c" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308631 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308632 13194139534764 true] [17592186308631 1089 "q-332552" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308631 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534764 true] [17592186308631 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-{x}^{2}-x-1.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to this equation given that the complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-x},$ where $A$ is an arbitrary constant." 13194139534764 true] [17592186308631 1113 #uuid "21fc98d5-a07a-53e9-b823-65887e0c4938" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308631 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{c}}{\\text{d}x}+{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$  we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-x-1\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\alpha {x}^{2}+(2\\alpha +\\beta )x+(\\beta +\\gamma )=-{x}^{2}-x-1\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\alpha =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 2\\alpha +\\beta =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\beta +\\gamma =-1\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,\\beta =1,\\gamma =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-{x}^{2}+x-2.\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nthe general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+x-2.\n$$" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308633 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308634 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308635 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308636 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308637 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1041 "selection" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308636 13194139534764 true] [17592186308632 1110 #uuid "42c0e438-2e2c-5a8e-abc3-67f8997c9f4d" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308633 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+x+2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308633 1111 #uuid "bf225a9f-68f4-5c7b-87f3-dfde75d31e24" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308634 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-2{x}^{2}+x-2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308634 1111 #uuid "dd622a14-745d-5bc4-82e9-e678a61adfea" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308635 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}+{x}^{2}-x-2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308635 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308635 1111 #uuid "7a20d413-26f0-53ee-bc1a-c4257a359af2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308636 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}+x-2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308636 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308636 1111 #uuid "2d19cfcc-2113-534f-87de-bc729ec24926" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308637 1034 "y=A{e}^{-x}-{x}^{2}-x-2" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308637 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308637 1111 #uuid "7bf58d12-f56b-5546-befb-36d9d93221da" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308638 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308639 13194139534764 true] [17592186308638 1089 "q-332756" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308638 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534764 true] [17592186308638 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+3y=-6x+1,\\,y(0)=\\frac{5}{3}\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+3y=-6x+1\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308638 1113 #uuid "d2079c55-b54d-5179-8b5d-5fa6fd0d212f" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308638 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+3{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-3x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\alpha +3(\\alpha x+\\beta )=-6x+1\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\alpha x+(\\alpha +3\\beta )=-6x+1\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\alpha =-6\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ \\alpha +3\\beta =1\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-2,\\,\\beta =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2x+1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}-2x+1.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=\\frac{5}{3}$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-3(0)}-2(0)+1 & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ A+1 & =\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ A & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-3x}-2x+1.\n$$" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308640 13194139534764 true] [17592186308639 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308641 13194139534764 true] [17592186308639 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534764 true] [17592186308639 1041 "field-1" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308639 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308640 13194139534764 true] [17592186308639 1110 #uuid "5dda6553-3ca9-5906-bdf1-513ea7bac620" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308640 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}e^{-3x}-2x+1" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308640 1111 #uuid "7fce7db3-d92c-5ce9-98d7-1a029894054e" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308641 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}e^{-3x}-2x+1" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308641 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308641 1111 #uuid "ece7ff4a-4703-5d30-a758-2d0eaa64f87a" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308642 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308643 13194139534764 true] [17592186308642 1089 "q-332782" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308642 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534764 true] [17592186308642 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+5y=10,\\,y(0)=1\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+5y=10\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308642 1113 #uuid "6ab36fa8-faf8-5e3a-8a1b-c1cff952273e" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308642 1145 "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+5{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-5x},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a constant. Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a constant, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\beta ,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\beta $ is a constant to be determined.\n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0.\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0+5\\beta =10\n$$\n\nSolving for $\\beta $ gives $\\beta =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-5x}+2.\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{0}+2 & =1 \\\\ A+2 & =1 \\\\ A & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=-{e}^{-5x}+2.\n$$" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308643 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308644 13194139534764 true] [17592186308643 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534764 true] [17592186308643 1041 "field-1" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308643 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308644 13194139534764 true] [17592186308643 1110 #uuid "2f821175-a091-589f-be58-2ee16889c49a" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308644 1034 "2-e^{-5x}" 13194139534764 true] [17592186308644 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534764 true] [17592186308644 1111 #uuid "9b887604-2cc7-5490-a98e-ba00780d40f2" 13194139534764 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-331913" 17592186308617 "q-331913/selection" 17592186308618 "q-331913/selection/01a694ae8c2e400a60563a72322b7de4a373d5dc6ee9b01a21efcd1c207da281" 17592186308619 "q-331913/selection/66a229dc667b5617bcbb1d4e4298a5bec5f4b42f6b64a49e859257b3ce28f710" 17592186308620 "q-331913/selection/6a071b534aebf45fcd195b8b75312a12e17d20e402230a6e8f738c70eba5bf59" 17592186308621 "q-331913/selection/858e498f5f64f52c2d9d775e2598674dc81b1441482e80e0697eac59124bcdce" 17592186308622 "q-331913/selection/d15a5d1d1ff36d403cfe682e83e05865057a3c32dddfcd849033ab8cdf05bdf0" 17592186308623 "q-332550" 17592186308624 "q-332550/selection" 17592186308625 "q-332550/selection/01920d15d82c5b1ff4fcf697f8a04b3dc69d9c08581077e14202f7a61fe5b645" 17592186308626 "q-332550/selection/4134ece82751b3b6a11925d1eca9bdab1f20c167e1aa58f953a48bc5b5345ab9" 17592186308627 "q-332550/selection/6831a43260bdcc843a214e09a034dc1f5a1ddbe14916d7cc2181d407c380de42" 17592186308628 "q-332550/selection/a5253ade8d39170937ce9df658ab3d6c872fa9ac4cc75de862194ea48328